On Thu, 29 Oct 2026 at 18:42 +0800, Zijun Hu wrote:
> QCA9377 is not ROME(QCA6174A), btusb driver does not support it,
> linux-firmware repo also does not have firmware it.
>
> See table @qca_devices_table for supported controllers from ROME.

Thank you, understood: QCA9377 is not a ROME part, and linux-firmware
has no QCA9377 USB firmware.

The kernel side is what I am unsure about. btusb lists three QCA9377
modules with BTUSB_QCA_ROME: 04ca:3015, 0cf3:e500 and 13d3:3503 (this
one). On 13d3:3503 the ROM reports rom_version 0x00000302, so
btusb_setup_qca() loads qca/rampatch_usb_00000302.bin and
qca/nvm_usb_00000302.bin, the files linux-firmware lists for QCA61x4
USB chips, and the patch version reads 0x3e8 afterwards (0x111 before).

Is that acceptable to Qualcomm for these QCA9377 modules? If not, what
should these three IDs get instead?

And separately: is there a known erratum in ROM build 0x111 for
transparent (mSBC) SCO? On its ROM firmware the controller stopped
answering HCI commands once such a link was streaming.

